(7439732, 1176024, 150277, '<td valign="top">Not even close the ones I thought could have been yours.  I enjoyed this image, gave it a 6 during voting.  If I had to try and pinpoint what kept it from being one of my favorites in the challenge, I felt a certain flatness in the mountains rather than the great depth I wanted to feel.  Still a perfect fit for wide-open, and deserved more imho.</td>', 'Not even close the ones I thought could have been yours.  I enjoyed this image, gave it a 6 during voting.  If I had to try and pinpoint what kept it from being one of my favorites in the challenge, I felt a certain flatness in the mountains rather than the great depth I wanted to feel.  Still a perfect fit for wide-open, and deserved more imho.', '2016-02-26 10:21:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439754, 1176109, 12611, '<td valign="top">Excellent job. Very "The Seventh Seal"  by Ingmar Bergman.</td>', 'Excellent job. Very "The Seventh Seal"  by Ingmar Bergman.', '2016-02-26 13:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439797, 1175954, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First off, congrats on the Top Ten finish.  Lovely scene, looks so cold - and I live in Canada so I know cold!  Great capture of tones of blue and grey, and that white glacier looks so pristine.  Great use of the available light and composition.  Really can''t fault this pic, but I am wondering why shoot so quickly for a landscape, unless you shot handheld.  <br/> <br/>Anyway please continue to enter and keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First off, congrats on the Top Ten finish.  Lovely scene, looks so cold - and I live in Canada so I know cold!  Great capture of tones of blue and grey, and that white glacier looks so pristine.  Great use of the available light and composition.  Really can''t fault this pic, but I am wondering why shoot so quickly for a landscape, unless you shot handheld.   Anyway please continue to enter and keep up the good work! Susan', '2016-02-26 18:47:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439804, 1176077, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is an inversion?  Never would have guessed.  Very good exposure, composition looks a tiny bit top-heavy with the clouds, but the darkness of the trees at the bottom helps balance it out somewhat.  Good conversion to b/w, some true black there in the trees and I see some pure white in the clouds but no vast bleached-out areas, with lots of great toning in between the two.  Don''t see any noise, and cropping it further wouldn''t help in a wide-open spaces challenge. I certainly think it should have scored higher, very sorry that it didn''t.<br/> <br/>Still, it''s a good shot, I do hope you keep entering!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is an inversion?  Never would have guessed.  Very good exposure, composition looks a tiny bit top-heavy with the clouds, but the darkness of the trees at the bottom helps balance it out somewhat.  Good conversion to b/w, some true black there in the trees and I see some pure white in the clouds but no vast bleached-out areas, with lots of great toning in between the two.  Don''t see any noise, and cropping it further wouldn''t help in a wide-open spaces challenge. I certainly think it should have scored higher, very sorry that it didn''t. Still, it''s a good shot, I do hope you keep entering! Susan', '2016-02-26 19:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439810, 1175989, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>As already noted by a commenter, this really does draw the viewer far and away.  Love the big dominant sky and the high super-white clouds, though none look bleachy, always a plus.  Then the well-seen stagger of rocks/cliffs coming towards the viewer from the bottom right, and that great final wedge of red sandstone helps seal the deal by tying together the dreamy blue of the sky, the denser blue-purple of the water and the little hint of green in bottom right.  Nicely done!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! As already noted by a commenter, this really does draw the viewer far and away.  Love the big dominant sky and the high super-white clouds, though none look bleachy, always a plus.  Then the well-seen stagger of rocks/cliffs coming towards the viewer from the bottom right, and that great final wedge of red sandstone helps seal the deal by tying together the dreamy blue of the sky, the denser blue-purple of the water and the little hint of green in bottom right.  Nicely done! Susan', '2016-02-26 19:51:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439926, 1176053, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Gorgeous b/w tones here, lovely scene, very picturesque. I love that you shot so fast and yet the sky has that blurry long-exposure look! The only thing I''m not crazy about is the lack of a truly dominant element.  The sky and mountains are competing with the forest and the open expanse of the foreground.  Almost a true 50/50 split.  I find the trees form a visual barrier between the mountains and foreground.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Gorgeous b/w tones here, lovely scene, very picturesque. I love that you shot so fast and yet the sky has that blurry long-exposure look! The only thing I''m not crazy about is the lack of a truly dominant element.  The sky and mountains are competing with the forest and the open expanse of the foreground.  Almost a true 50/50 split.  I find the trees form a visual barrier between the mountains and foreground. Hope this helps Susan', '2016-02-28 08:26:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439950, 1175954, 147059, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by snaffles:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First off, congrats on the Top Ten finish.  Lovely scene, looks so cold - and I live in Canada so I know cold!  Great capture of tones of blue and grey, and that white glacier looks so pristine.  Great use of the available light and composition.  Really can''t fault this pic, but I am wondering why shoot so quickly for a landscape, unless you shot handheld.  <br/> <br/>Anyway please continue to enter and keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Susan </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Susan for your constructive qritique, yes it was cold that day :) This shot was taken on my two day travel on a super jeep over the glacier, and then there is a lot of action going on and not always time to put up a tripod with filters and stuff. The shot was handheld and actually more like a snapshot, but turned out quite well.<br/> <br/>Thanks again and regards from Iceland<br/>Benni</td>', 'Originally posted by snaffles: Greetings from the Critique Club! First off, congrats on the Top Ten finish.  Lovely scene, looks so cold - and I live in Canada so I know cold!  Great capture of tones of blue and grey, and that white glacier looks so pristine.  Great use of the available light and composition.  Really can''t fault this pic, but I am wondering why shoot so quickly for a landscape, unless you shot handheld.   Anyway please continue to enter and keep up the good work! Susan   Thank you Susan for your constructive qritique, yes it was cold that day :) This shot was taken on my two day travel on a super jeep over the glacier, and then there is a lot of action going on and not always time to put up a tripod with filters and stuff. The shot was handheld and actually more like a snapshot, but turned out quite well. Thanks again and regards from IcelandBenni', '2016-02-28 10:57:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7440224, 1176080, 39427, '<td valign="top">Love this Mak!  Bringing me back to a place I visited long ago.  The humans for scale and story make it more than a pretty landscape, in classic Mak fashion.</td>', 'Love this Mak!  Bringing me back to a place I visited long ago.  The humans for scale and story make it more than a pretty landscape, in classic Mak fashion.', '2016-02-29 18:17:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7441195, 1176053, 25190, '<td valign="top">Wow the sky really adds drama too this images wonderful B&amp;W love the tones..</td>', 'Wow the sky really adds drama too this images wonderful B&W love the tones..', '2016-03-06 06:00:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7441743, 1176080, 43463, '<td valign="top">A late congrats on your Red! Love the beautiful tones, the light, and the mood of this fantastic shot Mak! The people walking along the path in the foreground really give a nice sense of scale while off in the distance I see another path that curves and winds towards St Michaels Mount. Stunning work!</td>', 'A late congrats on your Red! Love the beautiful tones, the light, and the mood of this fantastic shot Mak! The people walking along the path in the foreground really give a nice sense of scale while off in the distance I see another path that curves and winds towards St Michaels Mount. Stunning work!', '2016-03-07 16:56:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7441745, 1176059, 43463, '<td valign="top">Love the clever title for it perfectly suits the imagery! The silhouettes of the two people standing close to each other off in the ocean waters are enjoying the view of the wide expanse of sea and sky. The faithful dog stands on the shore anxiously awaiting for her/his people to return...one can almost here the dog''s confused thoughts "I am over here - why did you leave me here, the water is much better over here".</td>', 'Love the clever title for it perfectly suits the imagery! The silhouettes of the two people standing close to each other off in the ocean waters are enjoying the view of the wide expanse of sea and sky. The faithful dog stands on the shore anxiously awaiting for her/his people to return...one can almost here the dog''s confused thoughts "I am over here - why did you leave me here, the water is much better over here".', '2016-03-07 17:01:39.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
